// KQL reference queries for this app's Application Insights resource.
// Run these in the Azure Portal: App Insights resource -> Logs.
//
// This app doesn't have a live Application Insights resource in this environment (see README
// for what's real vs. simulated), but these queries are written against the real, standard
// App Insights schema (requests, dependencies) and are the same shapes that would have caught
// the /api/quotes/author-stats N+1 bug this piece diagnoses locally with Jaeger.

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Bonus deliverable: find endpoints that look like they have an N+1 problem —
// a request whose average dependency (DB) call count per operation is unusually
// high relative to its peers. A single grouped query does 1-2 DB calls per
// request; an N+1 query does one per row, so it stands out immediately once
// dependency counts are aggregated per request instead of looked at in isolation.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dependencies
| where timestamp > ago(1h)
| where type == "SQL" or name has "SELECT"
| summarize dbCallCount = count() by operation_Id
| join kind=inner (
    requests
    | where timestamp > ago(1h)
    | project operation_Id, name, duration, timestamp
) on operation_Id
| summarize
    avgDbCallsPerRequest = avg(dbCallCount),
    maxDbCallsPerRequest = max(dbCallCount),
    avgDurationMs = avg(duration),
    sampleCount = count()
    by name
| where avgDbCallsPerRequest > 10          // a handful of joins/lookups is normal; dozens-to-hundreds is not
| order by avgDbCallsPerRequest desc

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Simpler version of the same idea: slowest 10 requests in the last hour
// (this is what the Day 4 Piece 5 exercise deliverable already used — still the
// fastest way to spot a slow endpoint before digging into *why* it's slow).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
requests
| where timestamp > ago(1h)
| order by duration desc
| take 10
| project timestamp, name, duration, resultCode, success, cloud_RoleName, operation_Id

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Once a suspect endpoint is found (e.g. "GET /api/quotes/author-stats"),
// confirm the N+1 shape directly: many near-identical dependency calls sharing
// one operation_Id, each cheap on its own but numerous.
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dependencies
| where timestamp > ago(1h)
| where name == "GET /api/quotes/author-stats"
    or operation_Id in (
        requests
        | where name == "GET /api/quotes/author-stats"
        | project operation_Id
    )
| summarize callCount = count(), avgDurationMs = avg(duration), totalDurationMs = sum(duration) by operation_Id, data
| order by callCount desc

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Follow one request end-to-end across the app's own custom span and EF
// Core's query spans, by trace ID (same ID Serilog and Jaeger both use).
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
dependencies
| where operation_Id == "REPLACE_WITH_REAL_OPERATION_ID"
| union (requests | where operation_Id == "REPLACE_WITH_REAL_OPERATION_ID")
| order by timestamp asc
| project timestamp, itemType, name, duration, success
